PS5 IW620: no TDLS

The console's IW620 firmware rejects TDLS_OPERATION (0x122). A peer on the same network that starts a direct
link (an Android phone opening a page served by the console) then ends in "CMD_RESP: cmd 0x122 error", a
disconnect, and a scan command that never returns: Wi-Fi is gone until the driver is rebound. Without the
TDLS flags wpa_supplicant declines the request and the peer keeps going through the AP.
Applies after the ps5-linux-mwifiex patches.
---
diff --git a/mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c b/mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c
index 2ec7c88..3d24b52 100644
--- a/mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c
+++ b/mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c
@@ -12065,13 +12065,11 @@ mlan_status woal_register_cfg80211(moal_private *priv)
 #if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 4, 0)
 	wiphy->features |= NL80211_FEATURE_INACTIVITY_TIMER;
 #endif
-#if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 2, 0)
-	wiphy->flags |=
-		WIPHY_FLAG_SUPPORTS_TDLS | WIPHY_FLAG_TDLS_EXTERNAL_SETUP;
-#endif
-#if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 19, 0)
-	wiphy->features |= NL80211_FEATURE_TDLS_CHANNEL_SWITCH;
-#endif
+	/*
+	 * PS5: no TDLS. The console's IW620 firmware rejects TDLS_OPERATION (0x122); a peer's setup request then
+	 * ends in a disconnect and a scan command that never returns. Without these flags wpa_supplicant declines
+	 * the request and the peer keeps talking through the AP.
+	 */
 
 #ifdef STA_CFG80211
 #if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE > KERNEL_VERSION(4, 12, 14)
